  "solution": "The logic followed here is :** 1st number = 2 × (2nd number + 3rd number)**\n\nGiven :\n\n \n• (60, 17, 13)\n\n​60 = 2 × (17 + 13)\n\n60 = 2 × 30\n\n60 = 60 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (62, 14, 17)​\n\n62 = 2 × (14 + 17)\n\n62 = 2 × 31\n\n62 = 62 (LHS = RHS)\n\n​So,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (56, 15, 13)​\n\n56 = 2 × (15 + 13)\n\n56 = 2 × 28\n\n**56 = 56 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (43, 9, 12)​\n\n43 = 2 × (9 + 12)\n\n43 = 2 × 21\n\n**43 ≠ 42 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (55, 18, 9)​\n\n55 = 2 × (18 + 9)\n\n55 = 2 × 27\n\n**55 ≠ 54 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (57, 15, 14)​\n\n57 = 2 × (15 + 14)\n\n57 = 2 × 29\n\n**57 ≠ 58 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\nHence, **\"Option - (1)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n33:T12f7,\n&l",
